            <div xml:id="d687">

                <pb facs="0686" n="570" sameAs="frus:frus1915/pg570"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 365.117/116.</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">Ambassador Page to the
                            Secretary of State</hi>.</head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram.]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">American Embassy</hi>, <lb/>
                            <hi rendition="#italic">Rome</hi>
                        </placeName>
                        <date calendar="gregorian" when="1915-07-22">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">July 22, 1915</hi></date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>354. Department’s 287, July 20. Have brought Ghiloni case personally again to
                    attention Minister Foreign Affairs who promises to have matter studied promptly.
                    He seems more favorable than formerly to idea of naturalization.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Page.</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
